WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.110
Hello. I'm Ayumu Nishizawa, age 17.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.860
I was Hayate-kun's classmate before 
he transferred to Hakuo Academy.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.680
<b>Ayumu Nishizawa</b>

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.500
In other words...

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.970
In other words, I've known 
Hayate-kun longer than anyone else!

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:20.090
Um, Nishizawa-san, 
could you try to sound

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.450
more like you're having fun?

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.450
What?! I sounded bored?!

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.400
No, not so much bored as overzealous.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.720
Oh...

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.060
Okay, I'll try to sound more bouncy!

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:40.000
<b>Shiomi 
Municipal 
High School</b>

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:37.130
Uh... Something I like to do 
is eat Hayate-kun's cooking

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.360
at our part-time job.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.410
<i>All I can seem to talk 
about is Hayate-kun...</i>

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:47.140
<b>Hayate-kun's cooking is the best in the world!</b>

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.150
<i>If I keep this up, all of 
Japan will know I love him!</i>

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.440
<i>I love you, Ayasaki-kun.</i>

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:54.020
<i>Won't you please go out with me?</i>

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.360
Nishizawa-san? What's 
wrong? Are you hungry?

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.430
Wh— Hayate-kun!

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.480
You're gonna make all of Japan 
think I'm some sort of glutton...

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.110
<b>Gurgle</b>

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.930
Huh? I've gained three kilos...

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.400
Three... kilos?

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.490
No way, no way! That can't be right!

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:56.400
This has to be some kind of mistake!

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.290
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.410
<i>I don't look any different at all.</i>

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.640
<i>Even my skirt from last 
year's fall uniform still...</i>

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.500
<i>How did I suddenly put on three kilos?</i>

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.680
<i>What caused it?</i>

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.810
Morning, Hayate-kun!

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.610
Good morning, Nishizawa-san.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.120
<b>Changing</b>

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.120
Nishizawa-san.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.950
Would you like some of 
these meat buns I made?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.370
It's so good!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.640
I even made the dough myself.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.450
I'm pretty confident in them.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.780
I could eat tons of these!

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.420
Please have all you'd like.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.010
Okay!

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.510
Wait...

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.010
This is the reason!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:05.760
Sorry?

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.140
<i>The food you make for me 
every time I come to work...</i>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.390
There's no question! 
This has to be the reason!

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.450
<i>If I really steel myself 
and stop doing this,</i>

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.770
<i>my weight should return to normal.</i>

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:22.780
Sorry... I'll actually pass.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.840
The buns didn't suit your taste?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.560
Th-That's not it! 
Heck, I'll eat them all!

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.790
Oh, yes. I also baked cookies today.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:37.790
Help yourself.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:43.260
You said the ones I made for 
your birthday were good,

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.680
so I tried making some more.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.540
Hayate-kun...

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.180
That really did make me happy...

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.770
<i>A lot of things happened, but I don't 
think I'll ever forget that birthday.</i>

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:07.070
<i>My birthday is the one day of the year</i>

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.230
<i>when I can be the star unconditionally.</i>

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.660
<i>But the question is...</i>

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.920
<i>Does anyone even know 
today is my birthday?</i>

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.420
<i>Even Hayate-kun probably 
doesn't remember.</i>

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.580
Mm! That's good!

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:37.690
Oh, Hayate-kun, what are you 
making so early in the morning?

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.800
Oh, good morning, Maria-san.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.250
Today is Nishizawa-san's birthday,

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.560
so I made cookies for her present.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:46.450
Oh?

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.210
I can't spend a lot of 
money on a present,

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.160
so I'm at least putting 
my heart into it.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.950
Would you like to try one?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.590
Sure.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:57.210
Oh, it's good.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.550
Glad to hear it.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:04.260
Um, Hayate-kun, I'd like 
to ask you one thing...

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.180
Yes?

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.890
When is Segawa-san's birthday?

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.720
June 21st.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.110
And Asakaze-san?

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.610
July 31th.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.800
And Hanabishi-san?

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:13.970
September 9th.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:14.920
And Isumi-san?

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.310
September 24th.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.450
And Katsura-sensei?

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.730
November 10th.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:23.050
You're the kind of guy that girls love.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:23.740
Huh?

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:27.000
So today is the hamster's birthday?

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.950
Oh, Miss Nagi. Good morning.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.470
Did the sweet smell of 
the cookies wake you?

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:35.950
Stu— Of course not!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.120
Sweet! So sweet, Hayate!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.870
I thought you were 
cutting back on sugar...

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:42.820
I was talking about you!

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.680
A birthday doesn't mean you

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.880
just give someone a present
 and be done with it!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:47.980
What?!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.550
Well, your homemade cookies are too good

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.220
for the likes of that hamster...

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.200
But if you're going to do something,

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.920
you want her to be more 
grateful than necessary, right?

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.390
R-Right...

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:02.600
Then, why don't you 
throw her a surprise party?

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:04.510
Oh, Chiharu-san...

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.610
A surprise party, huh?

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.610
But that kind of thing 
is embarrassing...

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.890
It's when you get over 
the embarrassment and do it

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.600
anyway that it makes people happy!

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.070
But we have no 
obligation to go that far—

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.270
Don't compare 
friendship to obligation!

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.000
Don't you want to see 
your friend happy?!

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.830
But, but! If it doesn't make her happy,

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.750
we'll just look pathetic!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.010
If she's your friend, she'll be happy 
as long as you put your heart into it!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.180
Plus...

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:36.680
No matter what happens, this butler 
will take care of everything!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:37.690
Of course!

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.250
<i>She dumped it all on me!</i>

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.310
And so...

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.510
I've come up with this plan.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:45.060
<b>Nishizawa-san's Birthday 
Surprise Party Plan</b> 
 
When Nishizawa-san 
leaves the café after work, 
 
Everyone starts to 
decorate for the party  
 
Call Nishizawa-san 
back to the café 
 
 When she comes back, 
surprise!!

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:46.720
I see!

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.540
A surprise party, huh?

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:53.400
It's so great of you to plan 
a party for Ayumu, Nagi.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.310
It's not like that.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:59.080
Anyway, Nishizawa-san 
will be coming soon.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.080
Everyone should leave now, before she—

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.670
Huh? What are you all doing here?

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.460
<i>Crap! She's here already!</i>

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.450
<i>What do we do?!</i>

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.340
<i>We're in trouble right from the start!</i>

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.510
<i>I don't know why, but 
everyone's together.</i>

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.300
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.310
H-Hey, you guys...

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:24.230
Do you know what today, May 15th, is?!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.380
<i>Uh oh!</i>

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.310
<i>She just started pressing 
something really hard!</i>

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.030
M-May 15th is...

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.670
the day the War of the Spanish 
Succession began in 1701.

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.560
It's also the day Okinawa was 
returned to Japanese rule.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.200
It's a very important date in history.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.110
<i>Wow, nice follow-up!</i>

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:40.580
<i>Leave it to the student 
council president!</i>

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.210
No, that's not what I meant...

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.210
It's more like, the day 
something was born!

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.330
<i>No good! I can't follow that!</i>

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.340
<i>What do we do, Hayate?!</i>

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.400
Oh, that's right.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.840
Today, May 15th, is the day 
CoroCoro Comic was born, right?

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:56.840
<i>What?</i>

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.470
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:02.700
No, something closer to—

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.740
Well! I suddenly have something
 to do, so I've gotta go!

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:07.100
Uh, me too...

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.560
Wait... Hina-san!

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.680
<i>I won't lose!</i>

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:19.330
<i>I'll at least get Hayate-kun 
to remember my birthday!</i>

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:25.270
<i>But I don't have the audacity to 
just say, "Today's my birthday!"</i>

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.480
<i>So, what do I do?</i>

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.590
<b>The Outrage Newspaper
False Fortune Teller</b>

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.590
<i>That's it! The newspaper! 
If I use this...</i>

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:36.070
Hayate-kun! Is this today's paper?

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.120
Uh, yes, it is.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:42.220
Hmmm... So this is the 
paper for today, May 15!

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.570
Today's Taurus horoscope...

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:46.980
Watch for a sudden happening, huh?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.500
<i>How's that?</i>

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.940
Hello, this is Café Donguri...

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.470
<b>A Sudden Happening</b>

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:52.980
<i>He ignored me?!</i>

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.240
<i>But I can't give up!</i>

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:00.490
<i>There must be some way!</i>

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:04.700
<i></i>The weather report for today, May 15, is...<i></i>

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:04.700
<i>She's really trying to tell me 
that today's her birthday...</i>

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.060
<i>Another two hours until work is over...</i>

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:10.290
<i>I have to keep feigning ignorance!</i>

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.260
This is quite the psychological battle.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.010
Yeah. This will be one to watch.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.390
Oh, yeah... Hayate-kun!

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:22.890
Yes?

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.870
Today, I...

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.900
...brought a gift for the owner.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:34.410
Oh! That was nice of you.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.870
It's this. Do you think he'll like it?

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:41.520
If it's from you, Nishizawa-san,
 I'm sure he will.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:44.410
But I don't know how old he is,

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.080
so it was hard to choose something.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:49.420
<i>Not good!</i>

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.170
<i>This is heading toward...</i>

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:56.750
Th-That's true. He looks very young,

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.000
but I wonder how old he really is—

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.170
Frankly...

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.240
He won't tell me how old he is,

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.080
so I'd like to at least know his birthday.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.370
But I can't just come out and ask him.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:11.550
How do you think I could 
casually ask when his <i>birthday</i> is?

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:13.570
Oh no!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.870
She's trying to corner you, Hayata-kun!

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.190
What do you mean?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.230
I'm sure Hayata-kun realizes it,

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:23.380
but only one question generally comes 
to mind first in this situation...

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:27.080
What celebrity shares the 
same birthday as you?

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:28.610
That's what you'd ask.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:30.130
Now I get it...

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:33.580
So, from that point, the 
conversation will basically go...

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:36.890
Then, you should ask the 
owner what celebrities

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.150
have the same birthday as him.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:40.160
I see!

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:42.380
And then she'll casually say...

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:46.230
Oh, for me, it's the 
voice actress Eri Nakao-san.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:47.760
Hers is May 15th.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:49.730
...like that.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:53.030
It's common knowledge 
that the voice actress

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:54.540
Nakao-san was born on May 15th!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:55.980
He's about to slip!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.480
R-Really?

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.460
So, what will Hayata-kun do?

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:05.870
I-If you want to casually 
find out his birthday...

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:10.500
How about that?

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:12.460
Huh?

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:13.710
Huh?

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:17.700
Say you're practicing your 
English, and use it to ask.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:22.170
Then he'll tell you his 
birthday in English, right?

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:26.850
<i>Crap! I couldn't instantly 
say my birthday in English!</i>

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.080
Of course!

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.520
Excellent counter!

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:30.350
Yeah!

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:35.560
<i>All right.</i>

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:38.940
<i>Now the surprise party 
is sure to be a success.</i>

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.670
Well, I'm going on home, Hayate-kun.

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:45.570
Okay. Thanks for your hard work.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:13:00.550
I couldn't get Hayate-kun to 
realize it's my birthday...

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>I guess none of them 
care about me after all.</i>

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:13.430
Okay, everything's ready for the party.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.840
Shall we call Nishizawa-san back now?

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:16.690
Yes!

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.210
Indeed.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:18.860
Okay, Miss Nagi.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:21.490
Guess I have to...

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.820
Hello, this is Nishizawa.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:28.940
Hey, Hamster?

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:31.690
You forgot something at the café.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:34.370
It looks important, so come 
back and get it right now.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.790
What? I forgot something?

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:41.070
I'm really tired today. 
Just leave it there.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.710
H-Hey! It's important, 
so come and get it!

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.760
But...

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.670
Not good!

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:48.460
What do we do?

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.640
I said come and get it!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.470
But I said it's okay for today...

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.270
<i>If that's how it's gonna be...</i>

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.290
I'm telling you that I'm lonely because

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.770
I haven't been able to 
spend time with you lately!

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.850
If you get it, then come 
back and talk to me!

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:08.160
Wh-What was that all about?

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:12.660
What does she mean, 
go back and talk to her?

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:17.000
She's the one who forgot my birthday...

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.030
For goodness' sake...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.320
Okay, I came back for you.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.420
So what do you want to talk ab—

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:29.970
Huh?

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.640
Happy birthday!

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.140
Happy birthday, Nishizawa-san.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:37.780
Hayate-kun...

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:42.290
It's a surprise party just 
for you. Be happier.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:43.780
Here.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.590
Thank you! I love you, Nagi-chan!

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:53.580
Hey! Stupid! Get off me!

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:58.500
<b>Commercial Connecting Theater</b>

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.500
<b>Ceeeeasarrr
 Salad</b>

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.500
<b>Tacos!!</b>

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.500
<b>If you can eat it,
 that's enough</b>

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.520
<b>Duck cooked on a ceramic plate</b>

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.750
<i>Okay, I'm getting this!</i>

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.290
<i>This is great.</i>

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.510
<i>Having duck on the menu is so sensible.</i>

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.300
Excuse me...

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:12.560
I'd like the drink bar and the 
duck cooked on a chestplate—

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.390
That's "ceramic plate."

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:15.500
<b>O Cooked on a Ceramic Plate  
X Cooked on a Chest Plate</b>

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.020
Right...

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.520
The drink bar is over there.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.900
<b>Commercial Connecting Theater</b>

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:21.900
What? I'm not singing it!

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.480
I feel strange asking this of
 someone younger than me,

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.840
but I'll go for it.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.650
How can I get smarter?!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.100
How?!

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.660
That's easy.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.420
Just take this medicine.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.770
F.O.O.L. 
Pharmaceuticals

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:43.530
<b>Stu</b>

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:38.190
Idiot Distributors

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:37.870
Wh-What kind of medicine is that?

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.320
It's medicine for stupidity.

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.890
If a stupid person takes it,
 their stupidity heals,

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:43.540
and they become smart.

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:48.200
But if you get smarter by taking 
this, it proves your stupidity.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.840
Only take it if you believe 
you're hopelessly stupid.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:57.810
<b>Café Donguri</b>

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.810
Okay, you two can go now.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.130
Yes, sir.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.560
<i>That's right...</i>

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.560
<i>If we leave at the same time,</i>

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.060
<i>I can walk home alone with Hayate-kun.</i>

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:07.600
<i>Kashing!</i>

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:10.110
Well, I'm heading back 
to the mansion today,

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:11.570
so I'll be taking off, Nishizawa-san.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:13.750
Wait!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:18.200
J-Japan is a crime nation!

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.080
R-Right...

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.910
Evil Esper Organization

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:26.780
*This is only a depiction. 
May differ from actual evil esper organizations.

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:23.260
I heard yesterday that the myth of Japan's safety

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:26.410
was shattered and crimes have become cruel and vicious!

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:27.840
R-Really?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.620
So even the police are all 
talking about how dangerous

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:33.090
it is for a girl to be
 out at night alone!

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:36.280
Especially girls walking 
home from work alone!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.220
A girl! Walking home at night! <i>Alone!</i>

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.470
Oh, now that you mention it,

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:46.730
it is dangerous for a girl 
to be out at night alone.

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.590
So why don't I walk you 
home, Nishizawa-san?

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:54.900
Oh! Really? Thank you, Hayate-kun!

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:57.260
<i>What was that skit all about?</i>

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:09.460
<i>Oh, yeah. Maybe I should ask him 
if I look like I've gained weight.</i>

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:11.850
H-Hey, Hayate-kun...

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:12.790
Yes?

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:16.170
Your cooking is so good, 
I've been eating too much of it,

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:19.160
and I think it's made me 
gain weight recently.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.470
Really? You don't look any different.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:24.730
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:27.940
<i>If Hayate-kun didn't 
notice, I guess it's okay.</i>

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:31.020
But if it bothers you, 
would you like to run home?

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:31.870
Huh?

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:33.510
To burn off calories.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:35.730
Oh, yeah! That is one way!

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.560
<i>But if I do that, I'll 
be home in no time.</i>

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:41.820
<i>And we're walking home 
together, for once...</i>

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:47.460
Uh... I'll start running tomorrow.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.210
Okay.

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:52.110
Oh, yeah. How's school lately?

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.210
You're in the same class 
as Hina-san, right?

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.590
That's right.

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:58.370
So I have to work pretty hard.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:17:59.720
Hm? Why?

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:03.980
I don't want Hinagiku-san to 
hate me any more than she does.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:04.640
Huh?

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:07.480
Both at school and at the apartment,

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.730
I'm always causing trouble for her.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.980
You really think so?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.760
But acting cold is often

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.990
a way of expressing 
one's affection, right?

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:20.460
There's no way that 
kind of fantasy is true.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.030
That's why I need

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:26.490
to take things seriously, 
so I won't be a bother to her.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:30.970
<i>What kind of life have 
these two had at school</i>

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.960
<i>to create such a conflict between them?</i>

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.420
How's it going at Shiomi?

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:39.270
I guess I have more homework 
since I started my second year.

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.950
I have an assignment to 
turn in tomorrow, too...

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.240
Oh, crap!

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.510
Is something wrong?

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:47.210
Well, I left my notebook at school,

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.910
so I had planned to go back for it,

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:50.230
but then I forgot to do that...

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:52.770
Well, we're on our way home anyway.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.270
Why don't we stop there on the way?

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:59.000
<i>We'll be alone in the 
school at night...</i>

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:02.510
<i>I could confess under the moonlight,</i>

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:07.290
<i>or see a ghost and react by 
screaming and clinging to him...</i>

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:12.270
Oh! Yeah! Sounds like a 
nice idea, Hayate-kun!

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:19.980
It's easier to get in 
here than I expected.

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:20.930
True.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.060
The school really is kind of

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:25.900
creepy at night with 
nobody in it, though...

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.940
Don't worry. Unlike Hakuo, 
there are no ghosts here.

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:33.840
What? Hakuo has ghosts?!

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.520
Yes, and some pretty 
remarkable ones, at that.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.320
It's okay here, though...

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:39.520
Probably.

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:42.200
Probably?! What do you mean, probably?!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.780
Hey, Hayate-kun!

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:46.330
Oh, here it is!

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.830
I got my notebook, Hayate-kun!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:49.950
Oh, good.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:55.540
<i>I would be lying if I said 
I've never thought about it.</i>

00:19:55.950 --> 00:20:00.170
<i>Like, what if my parents 
hadn't sold me to the yakuza,</i>

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:03.680
<i>and I had continued to 
attend this school...</i>

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:08.220
<i>If she confessed that she liked 
me, as she did on that day,</i>

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:09.890
<i>would I...</i>

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.770
What's wrong, Hayate-kun?

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.030
It's nothing.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:23.070
Well, you got what you 
came for. Ready to go?

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:28.160
I'm a little disappointed, though.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.230
By what?

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:32.660
Well, here we are in 
the school at night.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:35.990
It seems like we should 
see a ghost or two.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.220
What makes you say something so scary?

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:44.550
<i>Then I could scream and 
cling to Hayate-kun...</i>

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:46.970
It is strange, though.

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:48.310
What is?

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:52.780
Well, I thought there would at least 
be a teacher here keeping watch.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.560
Now that you mention it, 
the classroom was unlocked.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:56.730
Yes.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:21:01.050
Surely a thief didn't break 
in and tie up the teacher...

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.550
What was that?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:07.990
<i>The myth is completely shattered!</i>

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:09.740
<i>Japan is a crime nation!</i>

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:11.590
Sensei! What happened?!

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:13.460
It wasn't really a thief, was it?

00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:17.270
Wait here! I'll get 
something to cut the rope!

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:20.020
Wait, Nishizawa! The thief 
is still hiding that way!

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:23.420
Nishizawa-san!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.980
Hayate Scryed!

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.520
Don't touch Nishizawa-san!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.030
She is...

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.690
very important to me.

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:47.530
Hayate-kun...

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.790
Are you okay, Nishizawa-san?

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.880
Y-Yes. Thank you.

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:55.410
But, your notebook...

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:58.790
Wait a minute! What are 
you guys doing here?

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.660
H-Hey, Hayate-kun...

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.330
Yes? What is it?

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:15.140
Um, about before...

00:22:16.070 --> 00:22:17.500
<i>She is...</i>

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:20.230
<i>very important to me.</i>

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:26.330
I think I might have lost some 
weight in all that chaos!

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:29.060
I wonder about that...

00:22:29.060 --> 00:22:30.820
Maybe not, huh?

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:08.510
Nice Cutie! Hey, hey!

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:10.720
Is it really necessary to do this?

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:12.470
I'm late for my event. Bye.

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:13.720
Wait! Wait!

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:15.300
Nice Cutie!

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:19.500
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!
